rt2800: enable MFP support unconditionally

rt2800lib sets MFP_CAPABLE only when hardware crypto is disabled through the
nohwcrypt module parameter. Without it, mac80211 strips the management frame
protection ciphers from the suites it advertises, so wpa_supplicant finds no
BIP cipher and WPA3-SAE is unreachable: SAE requires PMF. The driver now always
sets MFP_CAPABLE and refuses hardware keys for stations that negotiated MFP, so
mac80211 protects those connections in software while all others keep hardware
crypto.

Backport of:
  rt2800: enable MFP support unconditionally
    https://git.kernel.org/linus/b6b15e20421f

Upstream carries this from v5.8 on. The conditional MFP_CAPABLE it replaces
arrived in v4.7, so this one patch fits every kernel here from 4.7 on that
builds the driver.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ralink/rt2x00/rt2800lib.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ralink/rt2x00/rt2800lib.c
@@ -7488,9 +7488,7 @@ static int rt2800_probe_hw_mode(struct rt2x00_dev *rt2x00dev)
 	if (!rt2x00_is_usb(rt2x00dev))
 		ieee80211_hw_set(rt2x00dev->hw, HOST_BROADCAST_PS_BUFFERING);
 
-	/* Set MFP if HW crypto is disabled. */
-	if (rt2800_hwcrypt_disabled(rt2x00dev))
-		ieee80211_hw_set(rt2x00dev->hw, MFP_CAPABLE);
+	ieee80211_hw_set(rt2x00dev->hw, MFP_CAPABLE);
 
 	SET_IEEE80211_DEV(rt2x00dev->hw, rt2x00dev->dev);
 	SET_IEEE80211_PERM_ADDR(rt2x00dev->hw,
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ralink/rt2x00/rt2x00mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ralink/rt2x00/rt2x00mac.c
@@ -468,7 +468,8 @@ int rt2x00mac_set_key(struct ieee80211_hw *hw, enum set_key_cmd cmd,
 	if (!test_bit(DEVICE_STATE_PRESENT, &rt2x00dev->flags))
 		return 0;
 
-	if (!rt2x00_has_cap_hw_crypto(rt2x00dev))
+	/* The hardware can't do MFP */
+	if (!rt2x00_has_cap_hw_crypto(rt2x00dev) || (sta && sta->mfp))
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 
 	/*
